        },
        "delP1": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "Pa",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "First-level pressure thickness (Pa), the reference's first_level_pressure_thickness(PS) = -4.804826*P_unit + PS*0.015048, i.e. (Ap[1] - Ap[2]) + (Bp[1] - Bp[2])*PS on the GEOS-FP hybrid grid. jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/EarthSciDataExt.jl verbatim: Ap[2] = 4.804826 Pa; the constant was -0.04804826 until upstream found the hPa value had been inserted as Pa (100x too small)."
        },
        "Zagl": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "m",
          "shape": [
            "lon",
            "lat",
            "lev"
          ],
          "description": "Height above ground of the first level's MIDPOINT (m), the reference's first_level_midpoint_height(PS, T, QV, T2M, QV2M) = Rd/g0 * 0.5*(T*(1 + 0.61*QV) + T2M*(1 + 0.61*QV2M)) * log(PS/(PS - del_P/2)) with Rd = 287.05 J/kg/K, g0 = 9.80665 m/s^2 and del_P = delP1 (jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/EarthSciDataExt.jl verbatim): the hypsometric thickness of the lower half of layer 1 with the mean of the level and 2 m virtual temperatures. Only lev = 1 reaches deposition (Wesely gates every k_X on i_lev), so the column above is unused. Coupled into DryDepositionGas.z."
        },
