          "_comment": "d(CH3O2)/dt advection contribution, flux-form PPM in CWC mixing-ratio form: [-div(M q) + q div(M)]/m, with CH3O2's OWN lateral inflow halo bound to the rule's qbc params. operator_compose merges this with CH3O2's reaction tendency and the pointwise lift array-ifies the result. PLUS GEOS-Chem-style FULL PBL MIXING: pbl_f*(qbar_PBL - q)/tau_pblmix, where qbar_PBL = sum_k dp_k*pbl_f_k*q_k / sum_k dp_k*pbl_f_k. EXACTLY MASS-CONSERVING by construction -- sum_k dp_k*pbl_f_k*(qbar - q_k) = qbar*sum(dp*f) - sum(dp*f*q) = 0 identically, with the two sums being the same sums -- so the operator cannot create or destroy tracer no matter what pbl_f is. This is a CONTRACTION plus pointwise terms, NOT a stencil: it needs no vertical derivative and therefore no dz, which is what makes it expressible on this hybrid sigma-pressure grid where layer thickness varies with (i,j,t) and the library's varcoeff_laplacian_lev rule (1-D dz[k]) cannot apply.",
          "lhs": {
            "op": "D",
            "args": [
              "SuperFast.CH3O2"
            ],
            "wrt": "t"
          },
