            "nei_row",
            "nei_col"
          ]
        },
        "F_FORM": {
          "type": "parameter",
          "units": "1",
          "default": 0.0,
          "description": "NEI2016 FORM on the native 12US1 grid, in the file's own [TSTEP, LAY, ROW, COL] dim order (measured off the provider, not assumed). UNITS ARE A MONTHLY TOTAL IN SHORT TONS PER CELL despite the file's `tons/day` attribute and the loader's declared kg/m^2/s: the EPA gridded-merge monthly files store a whole month's emissions on a single 24-hour TSTEP. The ESM loader is pure I/O and converts nothing, so PHI_FORM below carries the whole chain (/days_in_month, short tons -> kg, / cell area). Same class of gap as F_PS's hPa-vs-Pa. See EarthSciData.jl issue #209.",
          "shape": [
