          "description": "NEI2016 FORM flattened onto the source-cell enumeration and converted to a flux density (kg/m^2/s, still carrying the month's total rather than a daily rate -- the /days_in_month is applied on the target grid): file value (short tons per cell for the month) x 907.185/86400 (EarthSciData to_unit's `tons/day` scale) / (dx*dy), then x cos(lat) for the planar-overlap area correction. The remaining /days_in_month is applied on the target grid, where it is one scalar rather than 137,241 of them. Includes emln_othpt (Canada/Mexico points), which GEOS-Chem reads as 2-D, so it shares the surface layer and is added on the source grid before the regrid.",
          "shape": [
            "ov.src_cells"
          ]
        },
        "E_FORM": {
          "type": "unknown",
          "units": "kg/m^2/s",
          "description": "FORM flux density (month-total basis) conservatively regridded onto the target grid: sum_i A_ij * PHI_i / A_full_j over the gated candidate set.",
          "shape": [
            "ov.tgt_cells"
          ]
        },
