    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "Transport3D.cloudFracc",
      "to": "WetDeposition.cloudFrac",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "EMEP wet-deposition driver, matching AtmosphericDeposition.jl couple2(WetDepositionCoupler, GEOSFPCoupler)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "Transport3D.rhoA",
      "to": "WetDeposition.rho_air",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "EMEP wet-deposition driver, matching AtmosphericDeposition.jl couple2(WetDepositionCoupler, GEOSFPCoupler)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "Transport3D.qrainc",
      "to": "WetDeposition.qrain",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "EMEP wet-deposition driver, matching AtmosphericDeposition.jl couple2(WetDepositionCoupler, GEOSFPCoupler)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "DryDepositionGas.k_O3",
      "to": "SuperFastDepositionSink.k_O3",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "First-order dry-deposition loss coefficient -> the SuperFast sink applicator. Species mapping mirrors jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/GasChemExt.jl couple2(SuperFastCoupler, DryDepositionGasCoupler): O3<-k_O3, NO2<-k_NO2, HNO3<-k_HNO3, H2O2<-k_H2O2, CH2O<-k_CH2O. NO is not dry-deposited (GEOS-Chem has no Is_DryDep flag for it)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "DryDepositionGas.k_NO2",
      "to": "SuperFastDepositionSink.k_NO2",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "First-order dry-deposition loss coefficient -> the SuperFast sink applicator. Species mapping mirrors jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/GasChemExt.jl couple2(SuperFastCoupler, DryDepositionGasCoupler): O3<-k_O3, NO2<-k_NO2, HNO3<-k_HNO3, H2O2<-k_H2O2, CH2O<-k_CH2O. NO is not dry-deposited (GEOS-Chem has no Is_DryDep flag for it)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "DryDepositionGas.k_HNO3",
      "to": "SuperFastDepositionSink.k_HNO3",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "First-order dry-deposition loss coefficient -> the SuperFast sink applicator. Species mapping mirrors jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/GasChemExt.jl couple2(SuperFastCoupler, DryDepositionGasCoupler): O3<-k_O3, NO2<-k_NO2, HNO3<-k_HNO3, H2O2<-k_H2O2, CH2O<-k_CH2O. NO is not dry-deposited (GEOS-Chem has no Is_DryDep flag for it)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "DryDepositionGas.k_H2O2",
      "to": "SuperFastDepositionSink.k_H2O2",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "First-order dry-deposition loss coefficient -> the SuperFast sink applicator. Species mapping mirrors jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/GasChemExt.jl couple2(SuperFastCoupler, DryDepositionGasCoupler): O3<-k_O3, NO2<-k_NO2, HNO3<-k_HNO3, H2O2<-k_H2O2, CH2O<-k_CH2O. NO is not dry-deposited (GEOS-Chem has no Is_DryDep flag for it)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "DryDepositionGas.k_CH2O",
      "to": "SuperFastDepositionSink.k_CH2O",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "First-order dry-deposition loss coefficient -> the SuperFast sink. CH2O uses k_CH2O (Hstar = 3.0e3, f0 = 1, the GEOS-Chem species database's values), not the legacy Wesely-table k_HCHO, which made v_d(CH2O) ~15x too slow; jialinl6/DepositionMTK.jl@cbe7d7db (branch superfast-gas-only) ext/GasChemExt.jl couple2(SuperFastCoupler, DryDepositionGasCoupler)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "WetDeposition.k_othergas",
      "to": "SuperFastDepositionSink.k_wet",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "Lumped soluble-gas wet-scavenging coefficient -> the sink applicator, applied to HNO3, H2O2, CH2O and CH3OOH exactly as couple2(SuperFastCoupler, WetDepositionCoupler) does."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "FastJX.j_H2O2",
      "to": "SuperFast.jH2O2",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "H2O2 + hv -> 2 OH. One of the six edges of the EarthSciModels coupling library couplings/fastjx_superfast.esm (roles Photolysis=FastJX, Chem=SuperFast), SPELLED OUT here rather than pulled in with coupling_import: a coupling_import `ref` is resolved by flatten against its `base_path` kwarg, which defaults to the process working directory (unlike a `models`/`reaction_systems` `ref`, resolved at load against the FILE's directory), so an imported edge would silently depend on where julia was started. These six replace SuperFast's fixed j-parameter defaults with the time/place/temperature-dependent Fast-JX rates, so photolysis now varies across the slice instead of being one hard-coded noon value."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "FastJX.j_H2COa",
      "to": "SuperFast.jH2COa",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "CH2O + hv -> CO + HO2 + H (radical channel)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "FastJX.j_H2COb",
      "to": "SuperFast.jH2COb",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "CH2O + hv -> CO + H2 (molecular channel)."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "FastJX.j_CH3OOH",
      "to": "SuperFast.jCH3OOH",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "CH3OOH + hv -> CH3O + OH."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "FastJX.j_NO2",
      "to": "SuperFast.jNO2",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "NO2 + hv -> NO + O; drives the NOx-O3 photostationary state, and so is the edge the O3 field is most sensitive to."
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "FastJX.j_o32OH",
      "to": "SuperFast.jO32OH",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "Effective O3 + hv -> 2 OH: j_O31D times the fraction of O(1D) that reacts with H2O rather than being quenched by N2/O2/H2 (FastJX.j_O31D_adj). This is why FastJX.H2O has to agree with SuperFast's H2O reservoir."
    },
    {
      "type": "operator_compose",
      "systems": [
        "SuperFast",
        "SuperFastDepositionSink"
      ],
      "description": "Add the deposition sink terms onto the SuperFast species ODEs. SuperFastDepositionSink carries one -(k_dry + k_wet)*X equation per species; operator_compose sums RHS contributions that share a dependent variable, so each species' chemistry tendency gains its loss term (dc/dt += -k*c). Placed BEFORE the SuperFast/Transport3D pointwise compose so the sink is already merged into D(SuperFast.X) when the lift array-ifies it. ORDER IS LOAD-BEARING: `systems[0]` is the merge TARGET and `systems[1:]` are the operators merged into it -- a match that has to RENAME the operator's dependent variable retargets it onto systems[0]'s spelling, deletes the other name from the state set, and rewrites every equation in the document off it (EarthSciAST `_apply_operator_compose!` / `_retarget_merged_names`). So the CHEMISTRY must be listed first. With the sink first, a sink written over its own species unknowns (rather than over scoped SuperFast.X references) matches only through the bare-name fallback, which renames SuperFast.O3 .. SuperFast.CH3OOH to SuperFastDepositionSink.* -- silently moving 7 of the 12 chemistry states out from under the transport and emission composes below, and out from under the runners' SuperFast.O3 lookups. This order is equivalent to the reverse for a sink written over scoped SuperFast.X references (verified: identical states and identical merged RHS), so it is correct against both spellings of the component. Per the component's own note this MUST be operator_compose, not a couple/additive connector -- the flatten pipeline silently discards the latter. The translate map names SuperFast's spelling of each shared species as the survivor (both components declare them as states, and EarthSciAST refuses a bare-name merge of two states since 2026-09-07).",
      "translate": {
        "SuperFast.O3": "SuperFastDepositionSink.O3",
        "SuperFast.NO2": "SuperFastDepositionSink.NO2",
        "SuperFast.HNO3": "SuperFastDepositionSink.HNO3",
        "SuperFast.H2O2": "SuperFastDepositionSink.H2O2",
        "SuperFast.CH2O": "SuperFastDepositionSink.CH2O",
        "SuperFast.CH3OOH": "SuperFastDepositionSink.CH3OOH"
      }
    },
    {
      "type": "variable_map",
      "from": "NEI2016Emis.flux_NO",
      "to": "NEIRegrid.F_NO",
      "transform": "param_to_var",
      "description": "NEI2016 NO LOADER field -> the native 12US1 array the regrid reads. Coupled from the loader field rather than the component's pointwise NO observed on purpose: reseact wants the whole source grid to regrid conservatively, not one bilinear sample at each 4x5 cell centre, which would draw a ~400 km cell's emissions from a single 12 km cell. Same shape of decision as GEOSFP.GEOSFP_I3.PS -> Transport3D.F_PS."
    },
